  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Smooth Manifolds\n\nA **smooth manifold** is a space that, *locally*, looks like $\\mathbb{R}^n$. Globally it can curve, twist, wrap around, or have non-trivial topology — but at every point there's a coordinate chart that lets you do calculus as if you were in $\\mathbb{R}^n$.\n\n**Definition** (informal). A smooth $n$-manifold is a topological space $M$ together with an **atlas** of charts $\\{(U_\\alpha, \\varphi_\\alpha)\\}$ where:\n\n1. $U_\\alpha \\subseteq M$ is open, $\\varphi_\\alpha : U_\\alpha \\to \\varphi_\\alpha(U_\\alpha) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^n$ is a homeomorphism.\n2. The $U_\\alpha$ cover $M$.\n3. **Smoothness compatibility**: for any two overlapping charts, the **transition map** $\\varphi_\\beta \\circ \\varphi_\\alpha^{-1}$ is smooth ($C^\\infty$).\n\nThe whole point: because transition maps are smooth, \"smoothness\" is a well-defined notion on $M$, independent of which chart you use.\n\nThis notebook walks the canonical examples — circles, spheres, tori — and the smooth-map calculus they support.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 21,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The unit circle $S^1$\n\nTwo charts cover $S^1 = \\{(x, y) : x^2 + y^2 = 1\\}$:\n\n- $U_1 = S^1 \\setminus \\{(0, 1)\\}$ (everything except the north pole), $\\varphi_1$ = stereographic projection from north pole.\n- $U_2 = S^1 \\setminus \\{(0, -1)\\}$ (everything except the south pole), $\\varphi_2$ = stereographic projection from south pole.\n\nThe transition map on $U_1 \\cap U_2$ is $\\varphi_2 \\circ \\varphi_1^{-1}(t) = 1/t$ — smooth on $\\mathbb{R} \\setminus \\{0\\}$.\n\nA simpler atlas uses angle: chart $\\varphi(\\cos\\theta, \\sin\\theta) = \\theta$ on $\\theta \\in (0, 2\\pi)$ and another shifted version. But this is just one example.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "theta_g : np_to_list(np_linspace(0, 2*float(%pi), 200))$\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"S¹ (unit circle)\",\n  lines(map(cos, theta_g), map(sin, theta_g)),\n  marker_size=10, color=\"red\", name=\"north pole (excluded from chart 1)\",\n  points([0.0], [1.0]),\n  marker_size=10, color=\"green\", name=\"south pole (excluded from chart 2)\",\n  points([0.0], [-1.0]),\n  title=\"Two charts cover S¹ — stereographic from each pole\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"y\",\n  grid=true, aspect_ratio=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 22,
      "outputs": [
        {
