    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The torus $T^2$\n\nThe product manifold $T^2 = S^1 \\times S^1$. Parametrise by two angles $(\\theta, \\phi)$ with the embedding $(\\cos\\theta(R + r\\cos\\phi),\\, \\sin\\theta(R + r\\cos\\phi),\\, r\\sin\\phi)$ for $R > r > 0$.\n\nTopologically: a doughnut. Locally diffeomorphic to $\\mathbb{R}^2$ everywhere, but globally has **non-trivial loops** that can't be contracted (one going around the centre hole, another around the tube).\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "R_outer : 2$ r_inner : 0.6$\nax_draw3d(\n  parametric_surface(cos(u)*(R_outer + r_inner*cos(v)),\n                     sin(u)*(R_outer + r_inner*cos(v)),\n                     r_inner*sin(v),\n                     u, 0, 2*%pi, v, 0, 2*%pi),\n  title=\"Torus T² = S¹ × S¹\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"y\", zlabel=\"z\",\n  colorscale=\"Picnic\"\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 24,
      "outputs": [
        {
